      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bbbf6aa17bab877dd8bc723|full_name}: Those statements definitely still stand! There are some memory leaks remaining here and there, but for the vast majority of the time, most of the RAM in use when VRChat is running is attributed to avatars loading and being held in memory until an opportunity to unload them arises. In comparison, the UI/system leaks are relatively small in magnitude.\n\nThis post was closed because it did not follow the standards for a bug report, not because the issue doesn't exist or has been \"solved\". As stated before, things like memory leaks are \"forever problems\".\n\n I have no issue if you (or the OP) wishes to re-open it following the standards given in http://bit.ly/vrchat-bug-reports, which is also present in the sidebar.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
